{"tiNastriRi triRi praTamamaDyamotamaH": [{"id": "tiNastrIRi trIRi praTamamaDyamottamAH", "headword": "तिङस्त्रीणि त्रीणि प्रथममध्यमोत्तमाः", "headword_slp1": "tiNastrIRi trIRi praTamamaDyamottamAH", "fold": "tiNastriRi triRi praTamamaDyamotamaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The three triads in both the sets परस्मैपद and आत्मनेपद , of conjugational affixes (comprised under the general name तिङ् , a प्रत्यहार formed of the first and last of them, viz. तिप् and महिङ्) are called, in order, Lowest - 3rd Person of European Grammar, Middle -2nd Person, and Highest -1st Person.\n\nTerms:", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["तिङस्त्रीणि त्रीणि प्रथममध्यमोत्तमाः १.४.१०१", "१.४.१०१", "१.४.१०१ तिङस्त्रीणि त्रीणि प्रथममध्यमोत्तमाः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["tiNastrIRi trIRi praTamamaDyamottamAH १.४.१०१", "१.४.१०१", "१.४.१०१ tiNastrIRi trIRi praTamamaDyamottamAH"]}], "tiNsitsarvaDatukam": [{"id": "tiNSitsArvaDAtukam", "headword": "तिङ्शित्सार्वधातुकम्", "headword_slp1": "tiNSitsArvaDAtukam", "fold": "tiNsitsarvaDatukam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "All the personal endings -- तिप्तस्झिसिप्थस्थमिब्वस्मस्तातांझथासाथांध्वमिड्वहिमहिङ् ३.४.७८, and all affixes with an indicatory श् are called सार्वधातुक ।\n\nTerms: सार्वधातुक", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["तिङ्शित्सार्वधातुकम् ३.४.११३", "३.४.११३", "३.४.११३ तिङ्शित्सार्वधातुकम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["tiNSitsArvaDAtukam ३.४.११३", "३.४.११३", "३.४.११३ tiNSitsArvaDAtukam"]}], "tiNasca": [{"id": "tiNaSca", "headword": "तिङश्च", "headword_slp1": "tiNaSca", "fold": "tiNasca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "So also after a finite verb, comes the affix तमप् (तम) when 'surpassing' is meant\n\nTerms: तमप् (तम)", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["तिङश्च ५.३.५६", "५.३.५६", "५.३.५६ तिङश्च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["tiNaSca ५.३.५६", "५.३.५६", "५.३.५६ tiNaSca"]}], "tiNo gotradini kut